* {{hyphenation|nl|kaap}}
* {{rhymes|nl|aːp}}

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|nl|frm|cap}}, from {{der|nl|pro|cap}}, from {{der|nl|la|caput}}.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|f|-en|kaapje}}

# a [[cape]], [[headland]]
#: {{ux|nl|[[Kaap de Goede Hoop]]|Cape of Good Hope|inline=1}}

===Etymology 2===
Perhaps related to {{m|nl|kopen|t=to buy, trade}}, possibly from {{der|nl|ofs|kāp||purchase}}, or otherwise from {{der|nl|la|capio|t=I seize}}. Attested before {{m|nl|kapen}}; originally only attested in the phrase {{m|nl|ter kaap varen}}.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|f|-en|kaapje}}

# [[privateering]], attacking and looting enemy ships under the auspices of one's government
#: {{syn|nl|kaapvaart}}
# the bird species [[European herring gull]], ''[[Larus argentatus]]'' {{rfv-sense|nl}}
#: {{syn|nl|zilvermeeuw}}

